## Raw memory

<mark style="color:purple;">`void`</mark> `memory.read(`<mark style="color:green;">`address`</mark>, <mark style="color:green;">`type`</mark>`)` -> <mark style="color:purple;">value</mark>

Reads a value from absolute memory address.

```lua
local value = memory.read(0x12345678, MEMORY_TYPE.int32)
local ptr = memory.read(0x12345678, MEMORY_TYPE.ptr)
local vec3 = memory.read(0x12345678, MEMORY_TYPE.vector3)
```

<mark style="color:purple;">`void`</mark> `memory.write(`<mark style="color:green;">`address`</mark>, <mark style="color:green;">`type`</mark>, <mark style="color:green;">`value`</mark>`)` -> <mark style="color:purple;">void</mark>

Writes a value to absolute memory address.

```lua
memory.write(0x12345678, MEMORY_TYPE.int32, 42)
memory.write(0x12345678, MEMORY_TYPE.float, 3.14)
memory.write(0x12345678, MEMORY_TYPE.vector3, vector3(1, 2, 3))
```

<mark style="color:purple;">`void`</mark> `memory.read_pointer(`<mark style="color:green;">`address`</mark>`)` -> <mark style="color:purple;">int64</mark>

Reads a 64-bit pointer from memory.

```lua
local ptr = memory.read_pointer(0x12345678)
local value = memory.read(ptr + 0x20, MEMORY_TYPE.float)
```

<mark style="color:purple;">`void`</mark> `memory.write_pointer(`<mark style="color:green;">`address`</mark>, <mark style="color:green;">`pointer`</mark>`)` -> <mark style="color:purple;">void</mark>

Writes a 64-bit pointer to memory.

```lua
memory.write_pointer(0x12345678, 0x87654321)
```

## Raw memory types

```lua
MEMORY_TYPE.int8       -- 8-bit signed integer
MEMORY_TYPE.int16      -- 16-bit signed integer
MEMORY_TYPE.int32      -- 32-bit signed integer
MEMORY_TYPE.int64      -- 64-bit signed integer
MEMORY_TYPE.uint8      -- 8-bit unsigned integer
MEMORY_TYPE.uint16     -- 16-bit unsigned integer
MEMORY_TYPE.uint32     -- 32-bit unsigned integer
MEMORY_TYPE.uint64     -- 64-bit unsigned integer
MEMORY_TYPE.float      -- Single precision float
MEMORY_TYPE.double     -- Double precision float
MEMORY_TYPE.ptr        -- 64-bit pointer
MEMORY_TYPE.vector2    -- 2D vector (2x float)
MEMORY_TYPE.vector3    -- 3D vector (3x float)
MEMORY_TYPE.vector4    -- 4D vector (4x float)
MEMORY_TYPE.bool       -- Boolean
```

## How to start

<div align="left"><figure><img src="/files/l20zfwK3N5WtknMl4Ap5" alt=""><figcaption></figcaption></figure></div>

To get started you need to use a software to analyze the memory, I would recommend re-class.

To reach the address, use the dex feature to copy the identity, which is the address.

If you want learn more about using re-class you can check it out here [here](https://www.unknowncheats.me/forum/league-of-legends/423786-reclass.html) or [here](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vQb21RM9-5M\&t=1s). Credits to the authors.

